{
  "format": "omission_inventory_v1",
  "request_sha256": "f5fdcb15827a485fb2cfe61ef3d9d34307597139c65509a4dcfa9176fb29d125",
  "chunks": [
    {
      "chunk": "c001",
      "status": "no_omission",
      "reason": "This chunk is the concatenation preamble: a bundle header, input-directory bookkeeping and a table of contents listing the four source files. Preamble is bookkeeping, not a source document, and cannot support an omission candidate. I identify no eligible missing fact here; this is my judgment, not a verified completeness claim.",
      "candidates": []
    },
    {
      "chunk": "c002",
      "status": "omission",
      "reason": "The NIH RePORTER abstract states several project-scope facts that I do not locate anywhere in the supplied record, including the >100,000 critically ill patient target framing, the ethics focus-group and contextual-factor activities, the enumeration of data types the network will acquire (including social determinants of health), the education/AI-literacy aim, and the collaboration structure. Novelty, applicability and support are unverified declarations.",
      "candidates": [
        {
          "id": "c002-patient-target",
          "kind": "omission",
          "source": "reporter_nih_gov_project-details-10472824_row7.txt",
          "quote": "Through 3 pillars, the CHoRUS data generation project will addresses multiple challenges relevant for acquiring an AI-ready data set from more than 100,000 critically ill patients",
          "target": {
            "owner": "",
            "slot_chain": ["updates", "update_details"]
          },
          "missing_information": "The abstract frames the planned acquisition target as an AI-ready data set from more than 100,000 critically ill patients. The record's updates.update_details carries only the project site's \"Anticipated Final Dataset\" figure of 100,000 patient admissions; the RePORTER statement of \"more than 100,000 critically ill patients\" (patients rather than admissions, stated as a project-plan challenge framing) does not appear in the record's update plan or elsewhere.",
          "scope_basis": "The declared scope owner is the root Dataset for the CHoRUS dataset; an anticipated acquisition magnitude stated as a project plan is information about that dataset's future state, which the record's updates slot already addresses for the anticipated snapshot."
        },
        {
          "id": "c002-ethics-focus-groups",
          "kind": "omission",
          "source": "reporter_nih_gov_project-details-10472824_row7.txt",
          "quote": "B) perform community-facing ethics focus groups to determine what data is appropriate for public sharing; C) ensure that data elements feature appropriate contextual factors such as geographic distance to the nearest hospital;",
          "target": {
            "owner": "",
            "slot_chain": ["notes"]
          },
          "missing_information": "Two planned project activities are absent from the record: community-facing ethics focus groups held to determine what data is appropriate for public sharing, and ensuring that data elements feature appropriate contextual factors such as geographic distance to the nearest hospital. The record's notes describe the Ethics pillar generically (community perspectives, trustworthiness, legal/regulatory analysis) but state neither the focus groups nor the contextual-factor requirement. Both remain planned/stated-as-plan statements in the source.",
          "scope_basis": "Both clauses describe how the CHoRUS dataset's content and public-sharing boundaries are to be determined, so they fall within the declared root Dataset scope; the record's notes slot is where the record already carries the project's pillar-level descriptions."
        },
        {
          "id": "c002-data-type-enumeration",
          "kind": "omission",
          "source": "reporter_nih_gov_project-details-10472824_row7.txt",
          "quote": "D) develop capabilities across a multi-center network to acquire, standardize, tokenize, store, visualize, and label data such as structured electronic health record data, tokenized unstructured electronic health record data, telemetry and EEG waveforms, imaging, and social determinants of health",
          "target": {
            "owner": "",
            "slot_chain": ["description"]
          },
          "missing_information": "The abstract enumerates the data categories the network is to acquire, including social determinants of health alongside structured EHR, tokenized unstructured EHR, telemetry and EEG waveforms, and imaging. The record's description enumerates the webinar table's data types but never mentions social determinants of health as a data category; the record carries only the RePORTER keyword \"social health determinants\". The record's labeling_strategies entry quotes the capabilities clause but stops before the data-category list.",
          "scope_basis": "The enumeration states what data the CHoRUS dataset is planned to contain, which is within the declared root Dataset scope and is the subject matter of the record's existing description slot."
        },
        {
          "id": "c002-education-aim",
          "kind": "omission",
          "source": "reporter_nih_gov_project-details-10472824_row7.txt",
          "quote": "F) cultivate expertise in the lay and scientific community to improve AI literacy nd utilization through multimodal educational approaches.",
          "target": {
            "owner": "",
            "slot_chain": ["purposes", "response"]
          },
          "missing_information": "A distinct stated project aim — cultivating expertise in the lay and scientific community to improve AI literacy and utilization through multimodal educational approaches (spelling \"nd\" as published) — is absent from the record's four purposes entries, which cover ML/AI data generation, the AI-ready dataset goal, ethically sourced datasets/tools, and the GitHub Network goal.",
          "scope_basis": "The declared scope owner is the root Dataset; this is an explicitly named purpose of the project that generates the CHoRUS dataset, and purposes is the record's multivalued slot for distinct source-named purposes."
        },
        {
          "id": "c002-collaboration-structure",
          "kind": "omission",
          "source": "reporter_nih_gov_project-details-10472824_row7.txt",
          "quote": "To accomplish this, the project will involve extensive collaboration between centers as well as through the NIH Bridge2AI program, the NIH Bridge2AI Bridge Center, external biomedical and clinical organizations, industry, and regulatory agencies.",
          "target": {
            "owner": "",
            "slot_chain": ["notes"]
          },
          "missing_information": "The planned collaboration structure — between centers and through the NIH Bridge2AI program, the NIH Bridge2AI Bridge Center, external biomedical and clinical organizations, industry, and regulatory agencies — does not appear in the record. The record's description notes only that CHoRUS is one of four data generation projects in the NIH-funded Bridge2AI consortium. This is a forward-looking (\"will involve\") statement and is not evidence that any collaboration was executed.",
          "scope_basis": "The clause describes the organizational context in which the declared CHoRUS dataset is to be produced, which the record already treats as notes-level contextual information about the root Dataset."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk": "c003",
      "status": "omission",
      "reason": "Most dataset facts in this slide deck (data types, standards, access control, counts, de-identification status, training/publication uses, registration) are already carried by the record. One stated element of the program purpose describing how the data are used is not. I deliberately do not propose the \"Bridge2AI CHoRUS Leadership Team\" slide as creator/maintainer content: a leadership listing does not establish a creator, maintainer or reviewer relationship for the declared dataset, and no governing list in this chunk assigns such responsibility.",
      "candidates": [
        {
          "id": "c003-multimodal-cohort-breadth",
          "kind": "omission",
          "source": "bridge2ai-for-clinical-care-informational-webinar-cohort-2_row9.txt",
          "quote": "intersection of healthcare challenges and AI/ML using multi-modal datasets from a broad range of cohort participants.",
          "target": {
            "owner": "",
            "slot_chain": ["intended_uses", "usage_notes"]
          },
          "missing_information": "The Program Purpose slide states that trainees conduct research at the intersection of healthcare challenges and AI/ML using multi-modal datasets from a broad range of cohort participants. The record's intended_uses[1].usage_notes carries the expanded-access, engagement/training/mentorship clause and the hands-on-training clause, but not this characterization of the data being used (multi-modal datasets from a broad range of cohort participants).",
          "scope_basis": "The clause describes the intended use of the declared CHoRUS dataset within the AIM-AHEAD training program, matching the record's existing intended_uses entry for hands-on AI/ML training under the root Dataset scope."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk": "c004",
      "status": "omission",
      "reason": "The training-overview slide names specific platforms and tool stacks on which the CHoRUS data are used during training; these are not stated in the record's intended_uses entry, which mentions only the Network, the data and tools generally.",
      "candidates": [
        {
          "id": "c004-collaborative-cloud",
          "kind": "omission",
          "source": "bridge2ai-for-clinical-care-informational-webinar-cohort-2_row9.txt",
          "quote": "Hands-on training on the Bridge2AI AI/ML for Clinical Care Collaborative Cloud",
          "target": {
            "owner": "",
            "slot_chain": ["intended_uses", "usage_notes"]
          },
          "missing_information": "The named platform on which hands-on training with the data takes place — the Bridge2AI AI/ML for Clinical Care Collaborative Cloud — is absent from the record. The record's intended_uses[1].usage_notes names only the \"Bridge2AI AI/ML for Clinical Care Network\"; the Collaborative Cloud platform is not stated anywhere in the record.",
          "scope_basis": "The platform is named as the environment in which the declared CHoRUS dataset is used by trainees, so it falls under the root Dataset scope and the record's existing hands-on-training intended use."
        },
        {
          "id": "c004-ohdsi-tool-stack",
          "kind": "omission",
          "source": "bridge2ai-for-clinical-care-informational-webinar-cohort-2_row9.txt",
          "quote": "Workshops on using the OHDSI tool stack",
          "target": {
            "owner": "",
            "slot_chain": ["intended_uses", "usage_notes"]
          },
          "missing_information": "The webinar states that training includes workshops on using the OHDSI tool stack (and, in adjacent bullets, on the OHDSI/OMOP common data model). The record mentions the OMOP Common Data Model only as a standardization target and never mentions the OHDSI tool stack as tooling used with the dataset by trainees. This is a statement about planned training content, not evidence that any specific tool version was applied to produce the dataset.",
          "scope_basis": "The clause concerns tooling used with the declared CHoRUS dataset in its training use context, matching the record's existing hands-on AI/ML training intended use under the root Dataset scope."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk": "c005",
      "status": "omission",
      "reason": "The eligibility slide states an organizational eligibility list governing who may participate in the program through which dataset access is granted; the record's access_review_process carries the registration steps and the \".edu\" email requirement but not this list.",
      "candidates": [
        {
          "id": "c005-eligible-organizations",
          "kind": "omission",
          "source": "bridge2ai-for-clinical-care-informational-webinar-cohort-2_row9.txt",
          "quote": "Eligible Organizations Higher education institutions Local, state, and tribal governments Nonprofits (with or without 501(c)(3) status) For-profit businesses and organizations Other U.S.-based organizations",
          "target": {
            "owner": "",
            "slot_chain": ["data_governance", "access_review_process"]
          },
          "missing_information": "The enumerated eligible organization types for the Cohort 2 program — higher education institutions; local, state and tribal governments; nonprofits with or without 501(c)(3) status; for-profit businesses and organizations; and other U.S.-based organizations — are absent from the record. The record describes the registration form, provisioning email and \".edu\" email requirement, but not the organizational eligibility governing the route by which program participants obtain access. The qualification that this list governs program eligibility (the slide heading is \"Eligibility Requirements\"), not dataset access in general, should be preserved.",
          "scope_basis": "The record already treats this program's access conditions as part of data_governance.access_review_process for the declared CHoRUS dataset, so the organizational eligibility list belongs to the same root Dataset scope and slot."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk": "c006",
      "status": "omission",
      "reason": "The project site states a tooling statement under its Data component, an NIH content disclaimer, and a named program-manager contact, none of which I locate in the record.",
      "candidates": [
        {
          "id": "c006-cloud-enclave-tools",
          "kind": "omission",
          "source": "chorus4ai_org_row11.txt",
          "quote": "The team creates tools to support the cloud enclave.",
          "target": {
            "owner": "",
            "slot_chain": ["notes"]
          },
          "missing_information": "Under the \"Data\" project component the site states that the team creates tools to support the cloud enclave. The record's description mentions the enclave only in the webinar's \"OMOP and telemetry in enclave\" sense, and its notes summarize the Ethics and People components but omit this tool-creation statement from the Data component.",
          "scope_basis": "The statement describes the Data component of the project that produces the declared CHoRUS dataset, which the record's notes slot already carries for the other two components under the root Dataset scope."
        },
        {
          "id": "c006-nih-disclaimer",
          "kind": "omission",
          "source": "chorus4ai_org_row11.txt",
          "quote": "The content on this website is solely the responsibility of the authors and does not necessarily represent the official views of the NIH.",
          "target": {
            "owner": "",
            "slot_chain": ["funders", "notes"]
          },
          "missing_information": "The funding attribution on the project site is accompanied by a disclaimer that the website content is solely the responsibility of the authors and does not necessarily represent the official views of the NIH. The record's funders[0].notes carries the award number and RePORTER record details but not this disclaimer.",
          "scope_basis": "The disclaimer is stated in the same sentence group as the NIH award attribution for the declared CHoRUS dataset's project, and funders.notes is where the record already carries that attribution context."
        },
        {
          "id": "c006-program-manager-contact",
          "kind": "omission",
          "source": "chorus4ai_org_row11.txt",
          "quote": "Contact Us\nCiera McCrary, MGH, Program Manager\ncmccrary@mgh.havard.edu",
          "target": {
            "owner": "",
            "slot_chain": ["notes"]
          },
          "missing_information": "The project site lists a named contact — Ciera McCrary, MGH, Program Manager, cmccrary@mgh.havard.edu (email spelling as published) — which does not appear anywhere in the record; the record's only contacts are the GitHub request-access addresses. The source identifies this person as a contact and program manager only; it does not assign creator, maintainer or reviewer responsibility for the dataset, so any placement should preserve that limited role.",
          "scope_basis": "The contact is published on the project site that the declared scope identifies as the dataset's own identifier and documentation source, so it is contact information about the root Dataset; notes is proposed because no source passage establishes a governance-committee or license-contact role."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk": "c007",
      "status": "omission",
      "reason": "The GitHub organization overview (historical documentation captured 2025-11-14) states several network-structure, standards-harmonization, status-tracking automation and developer-resource facts that I do not locate in the record, which carries other parts of the same page.",
      "candidates": [
        {
          "id": "c007-twenty-centers-fourteen-acquisition",
          "kind": "omission",
          "source": "github_chorus_ai_overview_2025-11-14.txt",
          "quote": "This collaboration spans 20 academic centers, of which 14 will contribute as Data Acquisition centers.",
          "target": {
            "owner": "",
            "slot_chain": ["notes"]
          },
          "missing_information": "The overview distinguishes 20 academic centers in the collaboration from the 14 that will contribute as Data Acquisition centers. The record separately carries \"14 different hospitals\" (project site and webinar) and \"60+ CHoRUS consortium members across 20 different institutions\" (anticipated snapshot) but never states this role distinction between the 20 academic centers and the 14 acquisition centers, nor its future-tense framing (\"will contribute\").",
          "scope_basis": "The sentence describes the contributing-site structure of the collaboration producing the declared CHoRUS dataset, which is root Dataset contextual information of the kind the record's notes and source_caveats already carry."
        },
        {
          "id": "c007-privacy-bias-sdoh",
          "kind": "omission",
          "source": "github_chorus_ai_overview_2025-11-14.txt",
          "quote": "Patient-focused efforts will determine the ethical and legal approaches to manage privacy and bias, while accounting for Social Determinants of Health.",
          "target": {
            "owner": "",
            "slot_chain": ["notes"]
          },
          "missing_information": "The overview states, as a future capability, that patient-focused efforts will determine the ethical and legal approaches to manage privacy and bias while accounting for Social Determinants of Health. The record's notes describe the site's Ethics component (community perspectives, trustworthiness, analysis of the legal and regulatory landscape) but do not state the management of bias or the accounting for Social Determinants of Health, and no known_biases entry exists.",
          "scope_basis": "The clause concerns the ethical and legal handling of the declared CHoRUS dataset's content, within the root Dataset scope; its forward-looking framing must be preserved as planned rather than applied."
        },
        {
          "id": "c007-unified-standards-harmonize",
          "kind": "omission",
          "source": "github_chorus_ai_overview_2025-11-14.txt",
          "quote": "Unified standards will harmonize multi-modal EHR, waveform, imaging, and text data.",
          "target": {
            "owner": "",
            "slot_chain": ["preprocessing_strategies", "preprocessing_details"]
          },
          "missing_information": "A stated future capability — unified standards harmonizing multi-modal EHR, waveform, imaging and text data — is absent from the record's three preprocessing_strategies entries (OMOP standardization, OHNLP tokenization of clinical notes, in-process EEG extraction) and from conforms_to. The statement is forward-looking (\"will harmonize\") and is not evidence that harmonization has been applied to this release.",
          "scope_basis": "Harmonization across the declared dataset's modalities is a processing/standardization method for the root Dataset, matching the record's existing multivalued preprocessing_strategies slot."
        },
        {
          "id": "c007-googlescript-status-automation",
          "kind": "omission",
          "source": "github_chorus_ai_overview_2025-11-14.txt",
          "quote": "We've created a GoogleScript that is triggered on each Google Form submission and makes calls\nto the GitHub API to update status and issue information appropriately. These site statuses\n\nend up in either the Standards Project or the Data Acquisition Project.",
          "target": {
            "owner": "",
            "slot_chain": ["extension_mechanism", "extension_details"]
          },
          "missing_information": "The record's extension_mechanism.extension_details states that sites submit status updates through the GitHub interface or a Google Form, but omits the stated automation: a GoogleScript triggered on each Google Form submission that calls the GitHub API to update status and issue information, with the resulting site statuses landing in either the Standards Project or the Data Acquisition Project.",
          "scope_basis": "This describes the contribution/status-tracking mechanism for sites supplying the declared CHoRUS dataset, the same subject the record's extension_mechanism already covers under the root Dataset scope."
        },
        {
          "id": "c007-developer-web-guide",
          "kind": "omission",
          "source": "github_chorus_ai_overview_2025-11-14.txt",
          "quote": "We have created a web guide for both contributors and users of the CHoRUS\n\nsoftware packages that compiles documentation in the chorus-developer repository.",
          "target": {
            "owner": "",
            "slot_chain": ["external_resources", "external_resources"]
          },
          "missing_information": "The overview names a web guide for contributors and users of the CHoRUS software packages, compiled in the chorus-developer repository (and, in the following sentence, a package status page listing versions and maintainers of CHoRUS packages). Neither the chorus-developer repository nor the web guide appears in the record's two external_resources entries, which name only the GitHub organization generally and the www.bridge2ai.org/chorus website.",
          "scope_basis": "These are named external resources associated with the declared CHoRUS dataset's tooling, matching the record's existing external_resources entries under the root Dataset scope. Nothing here is proposed as a processing-software version for this release."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "chunk": "c008",
      "status": "omission",
      "reason": "Although the prior receipt marked this chunk nothing_relevant, the repository listing names specific CHoRUS repositories whose stated descriptions concern the dataset's own extraction, de-identification-adjacent and characterization pipeline. A prior receipt judgment is not permission to skip review; these are declared candidates only, with support and novelty unverified.",
      "candidates": [
        {
          "id": "c008-extract-upload-repo",
          "kind": "omission",
          "source": "github_chorus_ai_overview_2025-11-14.txt",
          "quote": "chorus-extract-upload Public\n\nRepository with tools to create and upload a CHoRUS Data Extract",
          "target": {
            "owner": "",
            "slot_chain": ["external_resources", "external_resources"]
          },
          "missing_information": "The named repository chorus-extract-upload, described as holding tools to create and upload a CHoRUS Data Extract, is absent from the record. The record's external_resources[0] describes the GitHub organization only in general terms (software and tooling, semantic mappings, SOPs, project management overviews) without naming any repository. No version or applied-use claim is proposed; the listing states only that the repository exists with these tools.",
          "scope_basis": "The repository's stated function concerns creating and uploading the data extract that composes the declared CHoRUS dataset, so it is an external resource of the root Dataset in the same sense as the record's existing external_resources entry."
        },
        {
          "id": "c008-chorus-reports-repo",
          "kind": "omission",
          "source": "github_chorus_ai_overview_2025-11-14.txt",
          "quote": "CHoRUSReports\n\nPublic\n\nThis repo is dedicated to producing characterization reports to return to sites following their\ndata submissions",
          "target": {
            "owner": "",
            "slot_chain": ["external_resources", "external_resources"]
          },
          "missing_information": "The CHoRUSReports repository, described as dedicated to producing characterization reports returned to sites following their data submissions, is absent from the record, as is the existence of such a site-level characterization feedback step. The record documents the submission workflow and status tracking but not the return of characterization reports.",
          "scope_basis": "Characterization reports returned after site data submissions concern quality review of the contributions composing the declared CHoRUS dataset, within the root Dataset scope and the record's external_resources slot for named project resources."
        },
        {
          "id": "c008-uf-geocoding-repo",
          "kind": "omission",
          "source": "github_chorus_ai_overview_2025-11-14.txt",
          "quote": "UF-Geocoding Public\n\nForked from bihorac-LAB/Exposome\n\nOpen source code to geocode OMOP Location entities via DeGauss",
          "target": {
            "owner": "",
            "slot_chain": ["external_resources", "external_resources"]
          },
          "missing_information": "The UF-Geocoding repository, forked from bihorac-LAB/Exposome and described as open source code to geocode OMOP Location entities via DeGauss, is absent from the record. This listing names a tool and its stated function only; the chunk does not state that this code or any version of it was run on the declared release, and no such claim is proposed.",
          "scope_basis": "The repository is listed within the CHoRUS GitHub organization and its stated function operates on OMOP Location entities of the kind the declared CHoRUS dataset standardizes, making it an external resource of the root Dataset rather than evidence of an applied processing step."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
